    "durationMs": 151238,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21, Spring Data JPA, Flyway, PostgreSQL driver.\n\n**Code** (`src/main/java/bench/app/`):\n- `Link` entity + `LinkRepository` (findByCode, existsByCode, atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1`)\n- `LinkService` — validates URL via `java.net.URI` (must be absolute http/https with a host), validates custom codes against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`, generates 8-char random codes with collision retry, returns submitted URLs unchanged\n- `LinkController` (POST /links → 201, GET /links, GET /links/{code}) and `RedirectController` (GET /r/{code} → 302 + Location, increments exactly once)\n- `ApiExceptionHandler` — 409 duplicate code, 404 unknown code, 422 for malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code, all with `{\"error\": \"...\"}` bodies\n\n**Infra**:\n- `V1__create_links.sql` Flyway migration; schema fully owned by Flyway (`ddl-auto=none`)\n- `start.sh` parses `DATABASE_URL` (postgresql://user:pass@host:port/db) into `SPRING_DATASOURCE_*` env vars — no hard-coded credentials — then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; migrations apply at startup before the server accepts requests\n- README with a \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verification**: 29/29 smoke checks passed (all endpoints, all 422/404/409 cases, click-count exactness, list ordering). Restarted the server and confirmed clicks and data survived. Database truncated to a clean state, port 8000 free, no leftover processes."
